  "issues": [
    "The job requests 4 tasks via '#FLUX -n 4' but launches the `matlab` application as a single, serial process. Since the command is not prefixed with a parallel launcher like `flux run`, only one of the four allocated tasks will be used, leaving the other three tasks idle and wasting significant resources. If the MATLAB code is multi-threaded, the resource request should be changed to '#FLUX --ntasks=1 --cpus-per-task=4'. If the code is purely serial, the request should be '#FLUX -n 1'."
  ]
}
